From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 02:52:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] build: share incremental tsrs state and prune completed
 caches

Route typechecks and declaration builds through one tsrs runner. Cache
build info with declarations in atomic archives keyed by compiler, platform,
configuration, dependency locks, and build variant. Restore into independent
staging directories so builds can share state across compatible checkouts
without mixing public and internal outputs.

Keep failed and custom compiler runs out of shared publication, remove
declarations for deleted sources, and treat concurrent eviction as a miss.
Add project-scoped cache maintenance with configurable publication-age
retention while preserving temporary files, directories, and unknown data.

Document cache configuration and ownership, add focused real-compiler tests,
and run those Node suites separately from Vitest in CI.
